  "overview": {
    "en": "Julian Schwinger was an American theoretical physicist who shared the 1965 Nobel Prize in Physics for his contributions to quantum electrodynamics. He developed a rigorous, operator-based formulation of QED and made fundamental contributions to many areas of theoretical physics.",
