  "early_life": {
    "en": "Schwinger was born in New York City and showed extraordinary mathematical ability from an early age. He published his first physics paper at age 16 and earned his PhD from Columbia University at age 21 under Isidor Isaac Rabi.",
    "es": "",
    "pt": "",
    "fr": "",
    "de": "",
    "zh": "",
    "hi": "",
    "ar": "",
    "id": "",
    "ja": ""
  },
  "impact": {
    "en": "Schwinger's formulation of quantum electrodynamics provided the most rigorous mathematical framework for the theory and influenced generations of theoretical physicists. His development of source theory and effective action methods had lasting impact on quantum field theory.",
